# Intake & Sprint Governance

## Pipeline

```
ATI start (amounts)  →  /extract-calculations  →  artifacts/calculations/<module>-calculations.json
Transcript + docs (+ calc catalog)  →  /generate-brd  →  [Human: domain review]
       →  /plan-sprint  →  [Human: sprint approval]
       →  Seven delivery steps (Option A individually or Option B /deliver-sprint — see PIPELINE.md, EXECUTION-OPTIONS.md):
            1. /implement-api  2. /implement-ui  3. /expand-test-coverage → [Human: test-package Approved]
            4. /run-tests  5. /run-eval  6. /review-changes  7. /application-summary
```

## Human Gates (Required)

| Stage | Gate | Agent must |
|-------|------|------------|
| Calc catalog (blocking ASSUMPTION/CONFLICT) | SME | Do not claim formula parity `full` |
| BRD draft | Domain / PO review | Stop; set status **Draft — Pending Domain Review** |
| Sprint plan | Team / architect approval | Stop; set status **Proposed — Pending Approval** |
| Execution | Approved sprint only | Refuse `/deliver-sprint` and implement-* batch if plan not **Approved** |
| Test package | Human approval | `/expand-test-coverage` writes `docs/quality/test-package-review.md` as **Pending Approval**; refuse `/run-tests` (and `/deliver-sprint` resume) until **Approved** or dated waiver in `docs/harness/decisions.md` — agents cannot self-approve |
| Ad-hoc fixes | Human proceed | `/fix-issue` **defect** waits for explicit human **proceed** on the fix plan before implementation; ad-hoc bugs are not sprint SP items — do not route through `/deliver-sprint` |
| Cited incremental change | Change plan first | `/fix-issue` **cited-requirements** writes the change plan before code; human confirm only when scope or the catalog is ambiguous |
| BRD interpretation change | PO sign-off | Escalate; do not silently change meaning in code |

## Do

- Cite transcript speaker or document section for every new requirement
- Cite `CALC-*` from module calculation catalog for amount FRs
- On amount errors or source mismatch, **`<module>-calculations.json` is primary** (rule 32); do not “fix” the catalog toward Java/SQL/BRE
- Flag conflicts as DQ-xxx — never silently merge contradictory sources
- Version BRD on material change (`Version` header increment)
- Map sprint items to FR/BR IDs and execution commands

## Don't

- Skip intake because "we already have code"
- Auto-run `/deliver-sprint` after `/generate-brd`
- Lower test gates to close a sprint item
- Invent requirements **or amount formulas** to complete a BRD section

## Artifact Paths

See `config.yaml` → `intake`, `brd_drafts`, `sprints`, `artifacts.calculations`
